# CITATION.cff — RaceLoom-Bench v1.1.0 release metadata.
# Author-approved release information (final): version 1.1.0, author
# Ali Sarmadi, affiliation Tehran Institute for Advanced Studies, existing
# CFF default citation format, no ORCID (none supplied), and no DOI yet —
# the artifact DOI is added only after Zenodo creates it at publication.
# `date-released` is set to the actual UTC publication date of the
# v1.1.0 release.
# Note: the `license: MIT` field describes the original RaceLoom-Bench
# material. Third-party components (RaceLoom runtime, topology datasets)
# keep their own licenses; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and REUSE.toml.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: RaceLoom-Bench
message: >-
  If you use RaceLoom-Bench in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata below. RaceLoom itself is distributed separately and should be
  cited through its own artifact record (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.16884345).
type: software
authors:
  - name: Ali Sarmadi
    affiliation: Tehran Institute for Advanced Studies
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-05
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sarmadiali98/RaceLoom-Bench"
abstract: >-
  RaceLoom-Bench is a benchmark artifact for evaluating RaceLoom on
  software-defined networking race conditions. It contains RaceLoom model
  inputs, forwarding properties, topology assets, a canonical Docker
  execution pipeline, independent scientific result checkers, and expected
  result summaries for 16 principal B1-B4 configurations, 4 supplementary
  S1-S4 synthetic configurations, and 5 auxiliary smoke benchmarks.
keywords:
  - software-defined networking
  - race conditions
  - symbolic execution
  - benchmark
  - reproducibility
  - network verification
